@@ -126,3 +126,614 @@
  TAI_pc_global_component_commonwealth_desc: "Nearly every computer sold anywhere contains parts built here, under someone else's name. The volumes are extraordinary and the margins belong to whoever puts the badge on."
  TAI_pc_fragmented_margin_squeeze: "Fragmented Margin Squeeze"
  TAI_pc_fragmented_margin_squeeze_desc: "Too many capable firms chased the same shrinking market and undercut each other the whole way down. The engineering never stopped being good; the pricing never stopped falling."
+ # Operation Blue Tiger
+ TAI_can_pass_legislation_tt: "The government can carry legislation through the §YLegislative Yuan§!: it holds a majority, governs without a §YDivided Government§!, or has Stability above §Y60%§!."
+ TAI_blue_tiger_roots_ready_tt: "Has completed at least §Y3§! of: §Y$TAI_df_root$§!, §Y$TAI_na_rebuild_shield$§!, §Y$TAI_ss_root$§!, §Y$TAI_as_root$§!, §Y$TAI_pl_root$§!."
+ TAI_young_democracy: "Young Democracy"
+ TAI_young_democracy_desc: "Direct presidential elections are only four years old, and many institutions still carry habits from one-party rule. Public enthusiasm for democracy is high, but reform is slow and contested.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_df_political_dna$§! focus."
+ TAI_party_army: "Legacy of the Party-Army"
+ TAI_party_army_desc: "For decades the armed forces swore loyalty to the Kuomintang as well as the state. Many senior officers are uneasy about serving a government formed by another party.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will §GImprove§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_na_nationalize$§! focus and will be §RRemoved§! by the §Y$TAI_na_defense_act$§! focus."
+ TAI_party_army_reduced: "Legacy of the Party-Army"
+ TAI_party_army_reduced_desc: "The armed forces now serve the constitution in law, but old habits fade slowly.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! by the next §Y$TAI_na_defense_act$§! step."
+ TAI_did_legacy: "Defense-in-Depth Legacy"
+ TAI_did_legacy_desc: "Our forces were built to defeat a landing on the beaches. They dig in well but are poorly prepared to strike at sea or fight as a joint force.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will §GImprove§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_na_joint_command$§! focus and will be §RRemoved§! and replaced by a new posture through the doctrine focuses, such as §Y$TAI_na_outside_territory$§! or §Y$TAI_na_hard_roc$§!."
+ TAI_did_legacy_reformed: "Defense-in-Depth Legacy"
+ TAI_did_legacy_reformed_desc: "Joint command has removed the worst seams between the services, but our doctrine still centers on the beaches.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! and replaced by a new posture through the doctrine focuses, such as §Y$TAI_na_outside_territory$§! or §Y$TAI_na_hard_roc$§!."
+ TAI_uneven_reserves: "Large but Uneven Reserve System"
+ TAI_uneven_reserves_desc: "Millions of men are listed as reservists after conscription, but refresher training is short and irregular.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_na_reserve_reform$§! focus."
+ TAI_limited_absorption: "Advanced Procurement, Limited Absorption"
+ TAI_limited_absorption_desc: "The F-16s, Mirage 2000-5s and new frigates of the 1990s arrived faster than crews, mechanics and spare parts could keep up.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_na_absorption$§! focus."
+ TAI_divided_government: "Divided Government"
+ TAI_divided_government_desc: "The president's party does not control the Legislative Yuan. Every budget and reform must be negotiated with the opposition.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_df_legislative_reform$§! or §Y$TAI_su_pfp_reunite_blue$§! focus."
+ TAI_consolidated_democracy: "Consolidated Democracy"
+ TAI_consolidated_democracy_desc: "Peaceful alternation in power, independent courts and a free press are now accepted by every major party."
+ TAI_recession_relief: "Recession Relief"
+ TAI_recession_relief_desc: "Job programmes and targeted relief keep the technology downturn from becoming a social crisis."
+ TAI_technocratic_cabinet: "A Cabinet of Technocrats"
+ TAI_technocratic_cabinet_desc: "Experienced administrators run the ministries, trading political charisma for steady delivery."
+ TAI_professional_state_enterprises: "Experts, Not Loyalists"
+ TAI_professional_state_enterprises_desc: "State enterprises are led by managers chosen for competence rather than party service."
+ TAI_posture_active_defense: "Active Defense"
+ TAI_posture_active_defense_desc: "Our doctrine now aims to engage an invasion force in the Strait and at its bases, with air, naval and strike power taking the lead."
+ TAI_posture_hard_roc: "Hard ROC"
+ TAI_posture_hard_roc_desc: "Our doctrine emphasises survival, denial and recovery: hardened bases, mines and forces that can absorb a first strike."
+ TAI_posture_asymmetric: "Asymmetric Defense"
+ TAI_posture_asymmetric_desc: "Many small, mobile and survivable systems deny a stronger enemy control of our coasts, at the cost of peacetime presence in the air and at sea."
+ TAI_posture_hybrid: "Hybrid Resilience"
+ TAI_posture_hybrid_desc: "We keep enough conventional forces to contest gray-zone pressure while building survivable forces to deny an invasion."
+ TAI_professional_officer_corps: "Professional Officer Corps"
+ TAI_professional_officer_corps_desc: "Merit promotion and joint education build commanders for a changing force."
+ TAI_runway_repair_teams: "Runway Repair Teams"
+ TAI_runway_repair_teams_desc: "Trained crews and stockpiled materials can return damaged airbases to service within hours."
+ TAI_mined_approaches: "Mined Approaches"
+ TAI_mined_approaches_desc: "Mine stocks and fast minelayers make every landing beach dangerous for an invader."
+ TAI_hardened_shelters: "Hardened Shelters"
+ TAI_hardened_shelters_desc: "Aircraft shelters, buried command posts and spare runways help our forces survive the first strike."
+ TAI_dispersed_forces: "Dispersed Forces"
+ TAI_dispersed_forces_desc: "Units spread across many small sites cannot all be destroyed in a single salvo."
+ TAI_whole_of_society_defense: "Whole-of-Society Defense"
+ TAI_whole_of_society_defense_desc: "Reserves, civil defense volunteers and infrastructure operators train together to keep the island functioning under attack."
+ TAI_fortress_taiwan: "Fortress Taiwan"
+ TAI_fortress_taiwan_desc: "Every layer of our defense reinforces the others. Keeping it at readiness is expensive and politically demanding."
+ TAI_volunteer_reserve_split: "Volunteer / Reserve Split"
+ TAI_volunteer_reserve_split_desc: "Volunteers staff the first-line force while conscripts fill the reserves."
+ TAI_professional_force: "Professional First-Line Force"
+ TAI_professional_force_desc: "Long-service volunteers are better trained, harder to replace and more expensive to keep."
+ TAI_extended_conscription: "Extended Conscription"
+ TAI_extended_conscription_desc: "Long conscription keeps a deep pool of trained men at the cost of popularity and lost civilian work."
+ TAI_junior_leader_initiative: "Junior Leader Initiative"
+ TAI_junior_leader_initiative_desc: "Sergeants and lieutenants trusted to act on their own judgment make our force far harder to paralyse."
+ TAI_silicon_shield: "The Silicon Shield"
+ TAI_silicon_shield_desc: "Much of the world economy depends on our foundries, giving many governments a stake in our stability. It is an interest, not a guarantee."
+ TAI_financial_reform: "Financial Reform"
+ TAI_financial_reform_desc: "Cleaning up bad loans has restored confidence in our banks."
+ TAI_service_economy: "Services and Tourism"
+ TAI_service_economy_desc: "Finance, design and tourism earn income that does not pass through a single market."
+ TAI_strategic_fuel_reserve: "Strategic Petroleum Reserve"
+ TAI_strategic_fuel_reserve_desc: "Larger oil stocks buy time if tankers stop arriving."
+ TAI_strategic_reserves: "National Endurance Target"
+ TAI_strategic_reserves_desc: "Fuel, food and chip materials each have a stockpile target and a plan to reach it."
+ TAI_no_haste: "No Haste, Be Patient"
+ TAI_no_haste_desc: "Limits on large mainland investments slow growth and reduce our exposure to Beijing's leverage."
+ TAI_active_opening: "Active Opening, Effective Management"
+ TAI_active_opening_desc: "Looser investment rules let our firms profit from the mainland's growth while dependence rises."
+ TAI_direct_links: "Direct Cross-Strait Links"
+ TAI_direct_links_desc: "Direct shipping, flights and mail have ended decades of detours through Hong Kong."
+ TAI_cross_strait_framework: "Cross-Strait Economic Framework"
+ TAI_cross_strait_framework_desc: "A broad trade agreement lowers tariffs across the Strait and gives Beijing its strongest economic lever."
+ TAI_status_quo_dividend: "Status Quo Dividend"
+ TAI_status_quo_dividend_desc: "Calm in the Strait lowers insurance costs and attracts investors."
+ TAI_managed_ambiguity: "Managed Ambiguity"
+ TAI_managed_ambiguity_desc: "We decline to settle the final question while strengthening the state we already govern."
+ TAI_wto_membership: "WTO Membership"
+ TAI_wto_membership_desc: "As the Separate Customs Territory of Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Matsu, we now trade under global rules."
+ TAI_epidemic_preparedness: "Epidemic Preparedness"
+ TAI_epidemic_preparedness_desc: "The lessons of SARS have produced better surveillance, isolation wards and stockpiles."
+ TAI_representative_offices: "Representative Offices"
+ TAI_representative_offices_desc: "Economic and cultural offices abroad do the work of embassies without the name."
+ TAI_pacific_lifeline: "The Pacific Lifeline"
+ TAI_pacific_lifeline_desc: "Partners in Washington, Tokyo and Europe have crisis arrangements ready. None of them is an automatic promise to fight."
+ TAI_strategy_accommodation: "Strategy: Accommodation"
+ TAI_strategy_accommodation_desc: "Extensive economic ties and minimal confrontation bring prosperity while Beijing's leverage grows."
+ TAI_strategy_blue_tiger: "Strategy: Blue Tiger"
+ TAI_strategy_blue_tiger_desc: "Selective ties, diversification and preparation make Taiwan harder to coerce without provoking a crisis."
+ TAI_strategy_island_fortress: "Strategy: Island Fortress"
+ TAI_strategy_island_fortress_desc: "Rapid diversification and heavy stockpiling reduce our exposure at the cost of growth and a more alarmed Beijing."
+ TAI_civil_defense_drills: "Wan An Drills"
+ TAI_civil_defense_drills_desc: "Annual air-raid drills teach citizens where to shelter and how to help."
+ TAI_emergency_doctrine: "Blue Tiger Emergency Doctrine"
+ TAI_emergency_doctrine_desc: "Emergency procedures for gray-zone pressure, blockade, missile attack and invasion are written, rehearsed and bounded by law."
+ TAI_impossible_to_coerce: "Impossible to Coerce"
+ TAI_impossible_to_coerce_desc: "Taiwan does not have to be impossible to hurt. It has to be impossible to coerce at an acceptable price."
+ TAI_su_millennium_election: "The Millennium Election"
+ TAI_su_millennium_election_desc: "President Lee Teng-hui is barred from a third term, and the Kuomintang has split over his succession. Three serious candidates now compete for the first presidency of the new century."
+ TAI_su_heal_kmt_split: "Heal the KMT Split"
+ TAI_su_heal_kmt_split_desc: "James Soong left the Kuomintang to run on his own after Lee chose Lien Chan. Bringing his supporters back could unite the Pan-Blue vote, at the cost of reopening old quarrels."
+ TAI_su_voters_decide: "Let the Voters Decide"
+ TAI_su_voters_decide_desc: "We will not manipulate a divided field. The election will be decided at the ballot box, whoever the winner turns out to be."
+ TAI_su_lee_legacy: "Lee Teng-hui's Legacy"
+ TAI_su_lee_legacy_desc: "Lee dismantled the emergency constitution, opened direct presidential elections and described cross-Strait ties as a special state-to-state relationship. His successor inherits both the reforms and Beijing's anger."
+ TAI_su_peaceful_transfer: "The Peaceful Transfer of Power"
+ TAI_su_peaceful_transfer_desc: "Whoever won, the presidency must change hands under the constitution. A smooth handover proves that our democracy can survive a change of ruling party."
+ TAI_su_form_cabinet: "Form the Cabinet"
+ TAI_su_form_cabinet_desc: "The new president appoints a premier who must work with the Legislative Yuan. A cross-party appointment buys cooperation and reassures the officer corps."
+ TAI_su_minority_government: "A Government Without a Majority"
+ TAI_su_minority_government_desc: "We hold the presidency but not the Legislative Yuan. Budgets, procurement and reform will all have to be negotiated with the opposition."
+ TAI_su_unified_government: "A Unified Government"
+ TAI_su_unified_government_desc: "Our party controls both the presidency and the Legislative Yuan. We can legislate quickly, but critics will call it a return of the old order."
+ TAI_su_fourth_nuclear: "The Fourth Nuclear Plant Question"
+ TAI_su_fourth_nuclear_desc: "The Lungmen plant is already budgeted and under construction. Halting it would honor environmental pledges and provoke a constitutional fight with the legislature; finishing it secures power supply."
+ TAI_su_2001_recession: "Weather the 2001 Recession"
+ TAI_su_2001_recession_desc: "The technology downturn has pushed our export economy into its first contraction in decades. Targeted relief and job programmes can keep the slump from becoming a political crisis."
+ TAI_su_ly_2001: "The 2001 Legislative Election"
+ TAI_su_ly_2001_desc: "The People First Party and the Taiwan Solidarity Union now contest seats beside the KMT and DPP. A strong campaign can change the balance in the Legislative Yuan."
+ TAI_su_second_mandate: "Seek a Second Mandate"
+ TAI_su_second_mandate_desc: "The next presidential election will judge four years of divided government. We must run on our record and hold our coalition together."
+ TAI_su_heal_divided_island: "Healing a Divided Island"
+ TAI_su_heal_divided_island_desc: "A bitterly contested election has left many citizens doubting the result. Transparent recounts, court review and restraint on both sides can restore faith in the system."
+ TAI_su_second_test: "Democracy's Second Test"
+ TAI_su_second_test_desc: "The new single-member districts and a weary electorate may hand power to the opposition. Accepting defeat gracefully would show that alternation in power is now routine."
+ TAI_su_dpp_four_noes: "Four Noes and One Without"
+ TAI_su_dpp_four_noes_desc: "Provided Beijing does not intend to use force, we will not declare independence, change the national title, write state-to-state relations into the constitution, or hold an independence referendum, and we will keep the National Unification Council."
+ TAI_su_dpp_cautious_revolutionary: "The Cautious Revolutionary"
+ TAI_su_dpp_cautious_revolutionary_desc: "We came to office promising change but without a majority. A former KMT defense minister as premier and steady administration can win time for deeper reform."
+ TAI_su_dpp_taiwan_centered: "A Taiwan-Centered State"
+ TAI_su_dpp_taiwan_centered_desc: "Schools, museums and public life can reflect the island's own history and languages. Identity grows stronger, and Beijing watches every step."
+ TAI_su_dpp_referendum_act: "The Referendum Act"
+ TAI_su_dpp_referendum_act_desc: "Frustrated by legislative deadlock, we can give citizens a direct vote on public questions. Washington will judge each referendum by what it asks."
+ TAI_su_dpp_status_quo: "Reaffirm the Status Quo"
+ TAI_su_dpp_status_quo_desc: "We can promise Washington that referendums will not be used to change the island's status. Deep-Green activists will call it a betrayal."
+ TAI_su_dpp_name_rectification: "Name Rectification"
+ TAI_su_dpp_name_rectification_desc: "State enterprises and government bodies still carry \"China\" in their names. Renaming them asserts a separate identity and alarms both Beijing and Washington."
+ TAI_su_dpp_council_ceases: "The Council Ceases to Function"
+ TAI_su_dpp_council_ceases_desc: "Our earlier pledge depended on Beijing renouncing force. With more missiles aimed at us, we can declare that the National Unification Council ceases to function without formally abolishing it."
+ TAI_su_dpp_un_bid: "Join the UN as Taiwan"
+ TAI_su_dpp_un_bid_desc: "A membership application under the name Taiwan would rally our supporters and draw a public rebuke from Washington, which opposes unilateral changes to the status quo."
+ TAI_su_dpp_clean_party: "A Clean Green Party"
+ TAI_su_dpp_clean_party_desc: "We rose to power promising to end black-gold politics. Internal audits and open finances must apply to our own officials too."
+ TAI_su_kmt_rebuild: "Rebuild the Kuomintang"
+ TAI_su_kmt_rebuild_desc: "The 2000 split taught the party that it can no longer take power for granted. Reform must start inside the KMT itself."
+ TAI_su_kmt_party_assets: "Settle the Party Assets"
+ TAI_su_kmt_party_assets_desc: "The KMT's business empire was built while party and state were one. Selling or surrendering contested assets removes a constant source of scandal."
+ TAI_su_kmt_technocrats: "A Government of Technocrats"
+ TAI_su_kmt_technocrats_desc: "Experienced ministers and planners can deliver results that rallies cannot. Competence is our best answer to the charge of being the old regime."
+ TAI_su_kmt_pan_blue: "The Pan-Blue Coalition"
+ TAI_su_kmt_pan_blue_desc: "Cooperation with the People First Party and the New Party turns a divided camp into a working majority."
+ TAI_su_kmt_new_taiwanese: "We Are All New Taiwanese"
+ TAI_su_kmt_new_taiwanese_desc: "Lee Teng-hui's idea of the New Taiwanese welcomes every community that has made the island its home. It lets the KMT speak to rising local identity without abandoning the ROC."
+ TAI_su_kmt_roc_framework: "Preserve the ROC Framework"
+ TAI_su_kmt_roc_framework_desc: "We defend the Republic of China constitution as the common ground of the status quo. Beijing finds this easier to work with than formal independence."
+ TAI_su_kmt_peace_framework: "Toward a Peace Framework"
+ TAI_su_kmt_peace_framework_desc: "Regular talks and economic ties can lower the risk of war. Every agreement also deepens our dependence on the mainland market."
+ TAI_su_kmt_consent: "No Unification Without Consent"
+ TAI_su_kmt_consent_desc: "Whatever is negotiated across the Strait, no change to our status can take effect without the consent of the people of Taiwan."
+ TAI_su_kmt_us_ties: "Keep Washington Close"
+ TAI_su_kmt_us_ties_desc: "Better relations with Beijing must not look like drifting away from the United States. Quiet consultation keeps both doors open."
+ TAI_su_pfp_people_first: "The People First Government"
+ TAI_su_pfp_people_first_desc: "James Soong's new party now governs. It must prove it is more than one man's following."
+ TAI_su_pfp_provincial_network: "Mobilize the Provincial Network"
+ TAI_su_pfp_provincial_network_desc: "As provincial governor, Soong built ties with township leaders across the island. Those contacts can carry the new government's programme."
+ TAI_su_pfp_court_kmt_caucus: "Court the KMT Caucus"
+ TAI_su_pfp_court_kmt_caucus_desc: "Many KMT legislators share our outlook if not our party card. Committee posts and shared priorities can win their votes."
+ TAI_su_pfp_reunite_blue: "Reunite the Pan-Blue Camp"
+ TAI_su_pfp_reunite_blue_desc: "A joint ticket with the KMT would end the split that elected the DPP. It requires sharing power with old rivals."
+ TAI_su_pfp_clean_sweep: "The Clean Sweep"
+ TAI_su_pfp_clean_sweep_desc: "We can prosecute vote buying and factional graft even where our own allies benefit. Local factions will resist."
+ TAI_su_pfp_every_township: "Build Every Township"
+ TAI_su_pfp_every_township_desc: "Roads, drainage and schools in neglected townships turn goodwill into votes and better lives."
+ TAI_su_pfp_pragmatic_strait: "A Pragmatic Strait"
+ TAI_su_pfp_pragmatic_strait_desc: "We favour practical dealings with Beijing over symbolic confrontation, while keeping the ROC's sovereignty claims intact."
+ TAI_su_pfp_peace_mechanism: "A Cross-Strait Peace Mechanism"
+ TAI_su_pfp_peace_mechanism_desc: "A standing channel for crisis talks could prevent accidents at sea and in the air from becoming wars."
+ TAI_su_pfp_washington: "Reassure Washington"
+ TAI_su_pfp_washington_desc: "Washington must understand that dialogue with Beijing does not mean abandoning our security partnership."
+ TAI_df_root: "Consolidate the State, Not the Party"
+ TAI_df_root_desc: "Taiwan's democracy is young, and many institutions still bear the habits of one-party rule. Our task is to strengthen the state that every future government will inherit."
+ TAI_df_justice_minister: "A Reformist Justice Minister"
+ TAI_df_justice_minister_desc: "An incorruptible minister can promote younger prosecutors and protect them from political pressure, even when they investigate the ruling party."
+ TAI_df_unshackle_prosecutors: "Unshackle the Prosecutors"
+ TAI_df_unshackle_prosecutors_desc: "Allowing prosecutors to pursue cases beyond their home district turns rivalry between offices into a race to expose corruption."
+ TAI_df_professional_judiciary: "Professionalize the Judiciary"
+ TAI_df_professional_judiciary_desc: "Better training, evaluation and discipline for judges will slowly build public trust in the courts."
+ TAI_df_grand_justices: "Strengthen the Grand Justices"
+ TAI_df_grand_justices_desc: "A respected constitutional court can settle disputes between the president and the legislature before they paralyse government."
+ TAI_df_special_division: "A Special Investigation Division"
+ TAI_df_special_division_desc: "A dedicated unit for high-level corruption delivers fast results, but its power can be turned against political rivals."
+ TAI_df_ordinary_prosecutors: "Trust the Ordinary Prosecutors"
+ TAI_df_ordinary_prosecutors_desc: "Leaving high-level cases with regular prosecutors is slower but harder to politicise."
+ TAI_df_black_gold: "Clean Up Black Gold"
+ TAI_df_black_gold_desc: "Organized crime figures have sat in our legislature, and local factions have traded votes for public money. Breaking this system is a matter of national security."
+ TAI_df_vote_buying: "End the Vote-Buying Economy"
+ TAI_df_vote_buying_desc: "Prosecuting vote brokers and the candidates who pay them will cost some incumbents their seats."
+ TAI_df_sunshine_laws: "Sunshine Laws"
+ TAI_df_sunshine_laws_desc: "Asset disclosure and political donation rules let voters and journalists follow the money."
+ TAI_df_state_enterprises: "Experts, Not Loyalists"
+ TAI_df_state_enterprises_desc: "State enterprises should be run by managers chosen for skill rather than political loyalty."
+ TAI_df_farmers_associations: "Reform the Farmers' Associations"
+ TAI_df_farmers_associations_desc: "County farmers' associations have long channelled credit and patronage to local factions. Reform weakens those networks and angers rural power brokers."
+ TAI_df_special_funds_audit: "Audit the Special Funds"
+ TAI_df_special_funds_audit_desc: "Discretionary funds at the top of government invite abuse. Independent audits protect officeholders from temptation and from false accusations alike."
+ TAI_df_settle_executive: "Settle the Executive Question"
+ TAI_df_settle_executive_desc: "The constitution is ambiguous about who directs the cabinet when the president lacks a majority. A clear presidential reading ends a recurring crisis."
+ TAI_df_legislative_reform: "Reform the Legislative Yuan"
+ TAI_df_legislative_reform_desc: "Clear committee rules and procedures can make the legislature a place for bargaining rather than brawling."
+ TAI_df_end_sntv: "End the SNTV System"
+ TAI_df_end_sntv_desc: "Multi-member districts reward factional candidates and extreme positions. Single-member districts with a party list will reshape every campaign."
+ TAI_df_national_assembly: "The National Assembly Votes Itself Out"
+ TAI_df_national_assembly_desc: "Abolishing the National Assembly moves constitutional ratification to the voters and halves the size of the legislature."
+ TAI_df_control_yuan: "Protect the Control Yuan"
+ TAI_df_control_yuan_desc: "If nominations stall, the Control Yuan can sit empty for years. A confirmation compromise keeps the watchdog working."
+ TAI_df_civil_service: "A Neutral Civil Service"
+ TAI_df_civil_service_desc: "Officials who serve whichever party governs are the backbone of a stable democracy."
+ TAI_df_local_government: "Empower Local Government"
+ TAI_df_local_government_desc: "Capable county and city governments can keep services running when Taipei is under pressure."
+ TAI_df_civil_commissions: "Open the Commissions to Civil Society"
+ TAI_df_civil_commissions_desc: "Human rights, environmental and women's groups can sit on government commissions alongside business and officials."
+ TAI_df_party_tv_exit: "Get the Parties Out of Television"
+ TAI_df_party_tv_exit_desc: "Parties, the government and the military should not own broadcasters. Their exit from the airwaves strengthens media independence."
+ TAI_df_public_broadcasting: "Expand Public Broadcasting"
+ TAI_df_public_broadcasting_desc: "A well-funded public broadcaster offers a trusted source of news in a sensational media market."
+ TAI_df_every_community: "Voices of Every Community"
+ TAI_df_every_community_desc: "Hakka and indigenous broadcasting gives every community a voice in national life."
+ TAI_df_martial_law_past: "Confront the Martial-Law Past"
+ TAI_df_martial_law_past_desc: "Opening archives and compensating victims of the White Terror acknowledges a painful history. Some officers see it as an attack on the armed forces."
+ TAI_df_rapid_facts: "Rapid Factual Communication"
+ TAI_df_rapid_facts_desc: "When rumours spread faster than facts, the government must publish verified information quickly and plainly."
+ TAI_df_media_literacy: "Media Literacy for All"
+ TAI_df_media_literacy_desc: "Teaching citizens to check sources makes disinformation less effective without restricting speech."
+ TAI_df_influence_transparency: "Foreign Influence Transparency"
+ TAI_df_influence_transparency_desc: "Disclosure rules expose covert foreign funding of media and politics while leaving open debate untouched."
+ TAI_df_counter_disinfo: "Counter-Disinformation Center"
+ TAI_df_counter_disinfo_desc: "A government center can rebut false stories within hours. Critics fear it may decide what counts as truth."
+ TAI_df_political_dna: "Democracy in the Political DNA"
+ TAI_df_political_dna_desc: "Clean elections, independent courts and a free press have become habits that no party can easily undo. Our democracy is now a source of national strength."
+ TAI_na_rebuild_shield: "Rebuild the Shield"
+ TAI_na_rebuild_shield_desc: "The 1995-96 missile crisis showed that our defense was built for an invasion that might never come first. A national defense review must ask what we are defending against."
+ TAI_na_nationalize: "Nationalize the Armed Forces"
+ TAI_na_nationalize_desc: "Our officers must serve the constitution rather than any party. The change unsettles commanders raised under the old system."
+ TAI_na_defense_act: "Implement the National Defense Act"
+ TAI_na_defense_act_desc: "The National Defense Act unifies command under a civilian minister and makes political neutrality law."
+ TAI_na_reassure_commanders: "Reassure the Commanders"
+ TAI_na_reassure_commanders_desc: "Respecting professional judgment and seniority calms the officer corps, though it slows reforms they dislike."
+ TAI_na_officer_corps: "Professional Officer Corps"
+ TAI_na_officer_corps_desc: "Promotion by merit, joint education and modern staff training build leaders for a changing force."
+ TAI_na_political_warfare: "Reform the Political Warfare Department"
+ TAI_na_political_warfare_desc: "Political officers once taught loyalty to the party. Their new role is morale, welfare and constitutional education."
+ TAI_na_joint_command: "Joint Command Reform"
+ TAI_na_joint_command_desc: "The army, navy and air force must plan and fight as one force rather than three rival services."
+ TAI_na_reassess_did: "Reassess Defense-in-Depth"
+ TAI_na_reassess_did_desc: "General Hau Pei-tsun's Decisive Campaign at the Water's Edge aimed to defeat a landing on our beaches. Missiles can now hurt us long before any landing."
+ TAI_na_missile_crisis_lessons: "Lessons of the Missile Crisis"
+ TAI_na_missile_crisis_lessons_desc: "The 1996 missile tests closed ports and frightened markets without a single soldier landing. Our next investments must answer that kind of pressure."
+ TAI_na_outside_territory: "Decisive Campaign Outside the Territory"
+ TAI_na_outside_territory_desc: "We will engage invasion forces at their bases and in the Strait rather than wait for the beaches. After the election, the explicit preemptive option is dropped; the emphasis on air, naval and strike power remains."
+ TAI_na_effective_deterrence: "Effective Deterrence, Resolute Defense"
+ TAI_na_effective_deterrence_desc: "Putting deterrence first in our defense doctrine signals that active countermeasures now carry real weight."
+ TAI_na_air_sea_interdiction: "Air-Sea Interdiction"
+ TAI_na_air_sea_interdiction_desc: "Anti-ship aircraft, missile boats and coordinated strikes can attack an invasion fleet while it crosses the Strait."
+ TAI_na_hf2e: "The HF-2E Program"
+ TAI_na_hf2e_desc: "A domestically built land-attack cruise missile could threaten the bases an invasion would need. Beijing calls it offensive, some legislators oppose its cost, and Washington worries about escalation."
+ TAI_na_hf2e_extended: "Extended-Range Countermeasures"
+ TAI_na_hf2e_extended_desc: "Longer-range variants increase the number of targets we can hold at risk, and the political cost of building them."
+ TAI_na_info_warfare: "Information and Electronic Warfare Command"
+ TAI_na_info_warfare_desc: "Cyber defense and electronic warfare protect command networks that every other defense depends on."
+ TAI_na_layered_air_defense: "Layered Air and Missile Defense"
+ TAI_na_layered_air_defense_desc: "Patriot batteries, indigenous Tien Kung missiles and early-warning radar together reduce the damage a missile salvo can do."
+ TAI_na_harden_island: "Harden the Island"
+ TAI_na_harden_island_desc: "Hardened shelters, buried command posts and spare runways help our forces survive the first strike."
+ TAI_na_repair_runways: "Repair the Runways"
+ TAI_na_repair_runways_desc: "Rapid runway repair teams can return damaged airbases to service within hours."
+ TAI_na_mine_approaches: "Mine the Approaches"
+ TAI_na_mine_approaches_desc: "Sea mines and fast minelayers make every landing beach a gamble for an invader."
+ TAI_na_rapid_redeploy: "Rapid Internal Redeployment"
+ TAI_na_rapid_redeploy_desc: "Road and rail plans let reserves move quickly to wherever an enemy lands."
+ TAI_na_hard_roc: "Hard ROC"
+ TAI_na_hard_roc_desc: "Su Chi's Hard ROC concept emphasises survival, denial and recovery rather than distant strikes. Programmes already built remain in service."
+ TAI_na_mobile_fires: "Mobile Coastal Fires"
+ TAI_na_mobile_fires_desc: "Truck-mounted anti-ship missiles that hide and move are harder to destroy than fixed batteries."
+ TAI_na_disperse: "Disperse and Survive"
+ TAI_na_disperse_desc: "Forces spread across many small sites cannot all be destroyed in one strike."
+ TAI_na_unmanned: "Unmanned Systems"
+ TAI_na_unmanned_desc: "Cheap drones and unmanned boats can watch and strike across the Strait without risking crews."
+ TAI_na_odc: "Overall Defense Concept"
+ TAI_na_odc_desc: "Admiral Lee Hsi-min's concept invests in many small, mobile, survivable systems that deny a stronger enemy control of the littoral."
+ TAI_na_hybrid: "Hybrid Resilience"
+ TAI_na_hybrid_desc: "We keep enough fighters and ships to contest gray-zone pressure in peacetime while building survivable forces for invasion denial."
+ TAI_na_whole_of_society: "Whole-of-Society Defense"
+ TAI_na_whole_of_society_desc: "Civil defense, reserves and infrastructure operators train together so the whole island can keep functioning under attack."
+ TAI_na_fortress_taiwan: "Fortress Taiwan"
+ TAI_na_fortress_taiwan_desc: "Every layer of our defense now reinforces the others. Holding it at readiness is expensive and politically demanding."
+ TAI_na_manpower_question: "The Manpower Question"
+ TAI_na_manpower_question_desc: "We must choose between a smaller professional force, a large conscript army, or a balance of the two."
+ TAI_na_volunteer_reserve_split: "Volunteer / Reserve Split"
+ TAI_na_volunteer_reserve_split_desc: "Volunteers will staff the first-line force while conscripts fill the reserves."
+ TAI_na_professional_force: "Professional First-Line Force"
+ TAI_na_professional_force_desc: "Long-service volunteers are better trained and harder to replace. Recruiting them costs money every year."
+ TAI_na_extended_conscription: "Retain Extended Conscription"
+ TAI_na_extended_conscription_desc: "Long conscription keeps a deep pool of trained men at the cost of popularity and lost civilian work."
+ TAI_na_reserve_audit: "Reserve Readiness Audit"
+ TAI_na_reserve_audit_desc: "Our reserve rolls list millions of names, but how many could actually fight? An honest audit is the first step."
+ TAI_na_reserve_reform: "Reserve Reform"
+ TAI_na_reserve_reform_desc: "Regular refresher training and modern equipment turn a paper reserve into a real one."
+ TAI_na_nco_initiative: "NCO and Junior Leader Initiative"
+ TAI_na_nco_initiative_desc: "Sergeants and lieutenants trusted to act on their own judgment make a force far harder to paralyse."
+ TAI_na_territorial_defense: "Territorial Defense Brigades"
+ TAI_na_territorial_defense_desc: "Local brigades of reservists can defend their own towns and free regular units to counterattack."
+ TAI_na_us_links: "Secure U.S. Defense Links"
+ TAI_na_us_links_desc: "The Taiwan Relations Act lets Washington sell us defensive arms. It does not oblige the United States to fight for us."
+ TAI_na_2001_package: "The 2001 Arms Package"
+ TAI_na_2001_package_desc: "Washington has offered Kidd-class destroyers, P-3 patrol aircraft and diesel submarines it does not build itself. An offer is not a delivery."
+ TAI_na_special_budget: "Special Defense Budget"
+ TAI_na_special_budget_desc: "Major purchases need a special budget, and the opposition can delay, trim or block it."
+ TAI_na_kidd_destroyers: "Accept the Kidd-Class Destroyers"
+ TAI_na_kidd_destroyers_desc: "Four large destroyers bring area air defense to sea, along with crews to train and maintenance bills to pay."
+ TAI_na_maritime_patrol: "Maritime Patrol Aircraft"
+ TAI_na_maritime_patrol_desc: "Long-range patrol aircraft can track submarines through the Strait and its approaches."
+ TAI_na_submarine_question: "The Submarine Question"
+ TAI_na_submarine_question_desc: "The United States no longer builds diesel submarines, and European yards fear Beijing. We may have to build our own."
+ TAI_na_indigenous_submarine: "Indigenous Submarine Program"
+ TAI_na_indigenous_submarine_desc: "A domestic submarine programme will take many years and teach our shipyards skills no one will sell us."
+ TAI_na_interoperability: "Interoperability Without Alliance"
+ TAI_na_interoperability_desc: "Shared training standards and logistics with American forces improve readiness without any treaty commitment."
+ TAI_na_absorption: "Solve the Absorption Problem"
+ TAI_na_absorption_desc: "New equipment is useless without trained crews, spare parts and maintenance crews. We will fund the pipeline before the next purchase."
+ TAI_na_fighter_fleet: "Sustain the Fighter Fleet"
+ TAI_na_fighter_fleet_desc: "Our F-16s, Mirage 2000-5s and Ching-kuo fighters need upgrades and spares to stay ahead of the PLA Air Force."
+ TAI_na_idf_upgrade: "Upgrade the Indigenous Fighter"
+ TAI_na_idf_upgrade_desc: "An improved Ching-kuo with better avionics and weapons keeps our domestic aerospace industry alive."
+ TAI_na_csist: "Empower the Chungshan Institute"
+ TAI_na_csist_desc: "The Chungshan Institute of Science and Technology designs our missiles, radars and electronics. More funding means fewer dependencies."
+ TAI_na_gray_zone: "Contest the Gray Zone"
+ TAI_na_gray_zone_desc: "Fighters and patrol ships that meet every incursion show that our airspace and waters are watched, even when no shot is fired."
+ TAI_na_service_rivalry: "End the Service Rivalry"
+ TAI_na_service_rivalry_desc: "A joint budget process stops the army, navy and air force from fighting each other for every dollar."
+ TAI_ss_root: "The Silicon Island"
+ TAI_ss_root_desc: "TSMC and its rivals already lead the world in contract chipmaking. The question is whether that strength can protect the island as well as enrich it."
+ TAI_ss_deepen_hsinchu: "Deepen Hsinchu Science Park"
+ TAI_ss_deepen_hsinchu_desc: "More land, power and water for the science park keeps fabs and suppliers clustered together."
+ TAI_ss_southern_park: "Expand the Southern Science Park"
+ TAI_ss_southern_park_desc: "The Tainan science park spreads high-technology jobs to the south."
+ TAI_ss_central_park: "Found the Central Taiwan Science Park"
+ TAI_ss_central_park_desc: "A third science park near Taichung gives the industry room to grow."
+ TAI_ss_twelve_inch: "The 12-Inch Transition"
+ TAI_ss_twelve_inch_desc: "300-millimetre wafers cut the cost of every chip but require years of new tools and yield work."
+ TAI_ss_advanced_process: "Advanced Process R&D"
+ TAI_ss_advanced_process_desc: "Staying a node ahead of rivals keeps the world's chip designers coming to us."
+ TAI_ss_fabless: "Strengthen Fabless Partnerships"
+ TAI_ss_fabless_desc: "American and European design firms rely on our foundries. Long-term contracts make their success ours."
+ TAI_ss_itri: "Reinvest in ITRI"
+ TAI_ss_itri_desc: "The Industrial Technology Research Institute spun off TSMC and UMC. New funding can seed the next industries."
+ TAI_ss_crown_jewels: "Protect the Crown Jewels"
+ TAI_ss_crown_jewels_desc: "Our most advanced process knowledge stays at home. Partners may invest, license older technology and train engineers, but the core remains Taiwanese."
+ TAI_ss_supply_chain: "Protect Critical Supply Chains"
+ TAI_ss_supply_chain_desc: "Our fabs depend on Japanese chemicals, Dutch lithography and American tools. Mapping those dependencies is the first step to protecting them."
+ TAI_ss_materials_inventory: "Strategic Materials Inventory"
+ TAI_ss_materials_inventory_desc: "Stockpiles of wafers, gases and specialty chemicals let the fabs keep running if deliveries stop."
+ TAI_ss_us_compact: "U.S.-Taiwan Semiconductor Compact"
+ TAI_ss_us_compact_desc: "This alternate-history compact ties American capital and customers to our fabs while the leading-edge know-how stays here."
+ TAI_ss_court_berlin: "Court Berlin"
+ TAI_ss_court_berlin_desc: "German precision engineering, specialty materials and optics suppliers are vital links in our supply chain. This alternate-history push deepens those ties."
+ TAI_ss_dutch_litho: "Dutch Lithography Partnership"
+ TAI_ss_dutch_litho_desc: "Lithography machines are made by very few firms. Service agreements and spare parts keep our most valuable tools running."
+ TAI_ss_japan_materials: "Japanese Materials Alliance"
+ TAI_ss_japan_materials_desc: "Japanese firms supply many of the wafers, photoresists and chemicals our fabs consume."
+ TAI_ss_silicon_shield: "The Silicon Shield"
+ TAI_ss_silicon_shield_desc: "The world economy now depends on our foundries, giving many governments a stake in our stability. That interest is not a guarantee: a blockade can still cut the supplies our fabs need."
+ TAI_ss_trading_economy: "The Island Trading Economy"
+ TAI_ss_trading_economy_desc: "Almost everything we eat, burn and build passes through our ports. Trade is our lifeblood and our weak point."
+ TAI_ss_bad_loans: "Clear the Bad Loans"
+ TAI_ss_bad_loans_desc: "Non-performing loans weigh on our banks after years of easy credit. Writing them off now restores confidence."
+ TAI_ss_bank_consolidation: "Consolidate the Banks"
+ TAI_ss_bank_consolidation_desc: "Too many small banks compete for the same customers. Mergers create institutions able to weather a crisis."
+ TAI_ss_challenge_2008: "Challenge 2008"
+ TAI_ss_challenge_2008_desc: "A six-year national development plan sets targets for research, digital government and infrastructure."
+ TAI_ss_ten_projects: "Ten New Major Construction Projects"
+ TAI_ss_ten_projects_desc: "Ports, rail and research parks built now will serve the economy for decades."
+ TAI_ss_high_speed_rail: "Finish the High-Speed Rail"
+ TAI_ss_high_speed_rail_desc: "A bullet train from Taipei to Kaohsiung ties the west coast into one economy. It cannot open before its tracks are finished."
+ TAI_ss_e_taiwan: "e-Taiwan"
+ TAI_ss_e_taiwan_desc: "Broadband, digital government and online services make the state faster and the economy more productive."
+ TAI_ss_biotech: "Biotech Takeoff"
+ TAI_ss_biotech_desc: "Biotechnology diversifies our exports beyond electronics."
+ TAI_ss_services: "Services and Tourism"
+ TAI_ss_services_desc: "Finance, design and tourism earn income that does not pass through a single market."
+ TAI_ss_export_markets: "Diversify Export Markets"
+ TAI_ss_export_markets_desc: "New customers in Southeast Asia, Europe and the Americas reduce our exposure to any single buyer."
+ TAI_ss_fx_facility: "A Defined Reserve Facility"
+ TAI_ss_fx_facility_desc: "Our central bank holds large foreign reserves, but they are not a government piggy bank. Clear rules decide when they may defend the currency or pay for emergency imports."
+ TAI_ss_marine_insurance: "National Marine Insurance Pool"
+ TAI_ss_marine_insurance_desc: "If private insurers flee during a crisis, a state-backed pool can keep cargo moving. It is a contingent liability, not free money."
+ TAI_ss_energy_review: "Energy Security Review"
+ TAI_ss_energy_review_desc: "We import nearly all of our energy. A review shows how long we could last if tankers stopped coming."
+ TAI_ss_spr: "Strategic Petroleum Reserve"
+ TAI_ss_spr_desc: "Larger oil stocks buy time in a blockade. Tanks must be built and then filled before they help."
+ TAI_ss_lng: "Expand the LNG Terminals"
+ TAI_ss_lng_desc: "More gas terminals diversify the fuels our power plants burn."
+ TAI_ss_coal_stocks: "Coal Stockpiles for the Grid"
+ TAI_ss_coal_stocks_desc: "Coal yards at the power stations keep the lights on through short interruptions."
+ TAI_ss_renewables: "Renewable Energy Act"
+ TAI_ss_renewables_desc: "Wind and solar power give us a small share of energy that no blockade can cut."
+ TAI_ss_food_reserve: "National Food Reserve"
+ TAI_ss_food_reserve_desc: "Rice reserves and feed stocks protect against both bad harvests and blockade."
+ TAI_ss_wto_farmers: "Protect Farmers After the WTO"
+ TAI_ss_wto_farmers_desc: "Joining the WTO opens our market to cheaper imports. Support for farmers keeps domestic food production alive."
+ TAI_ss_emergency_shipping: "Emergency Shipping Arrangements"
+ TAI_ss_emergency_shipping_desc: "Reserved charter contracts give us ships to call on when commercial carriers hesitate."
+ TAI_ss_endurance_target: "A National Endurance Target"
+ TAI_ss_endurance_target_desc: "Fuel, food and chip materials each get a stockpile target and a plan to reach it."
+ TAI_as_root: "Across the Strait"
+ TAI_as_root_desc: "Trade and investment across the Strait keep growing even while political relations freeze. We must manage both at once."
+ TAI_as_go_slow: "No Haste, Be Patient"
+ TAI_as_go_slow_desc: "Lee Teng-hui's policy limited large investments on the mainland to avoid dependence. Keeping it means slower growth and less exposure."
+ TAI_as_active_opening: "Active Opening, Effective Management"
+ TAI_as_active_opening_desc: "Loosening investment limits lets our firms profit from the mainland's growth while the government watches the risks."
+ TAI_as_mini_three_links: "The Mini Three Links"
+ TAI_as_mini_three_links_desc: "Direct ferries, trade and mail between Kinmen, Matsu and Fujian are a modest first step toward normal links."
+ TAI_as_taishang: "The Taishang Question"
+ TAI_as_taishang_desc: "Hundreds of thousands of our businesspeople now live on the mainland. They bring home profits and also lobby for Beijing's preferences."
+ TAI_as_charter_flights: "Holiday Charter Flights"
+ TAI_as_charter_flights_desc: "Charter flights at Lunar New Year let families travel without changing planes in Hong Kong."
+ TAI_as_investment_caps: "Sector Investment Caps"
+ TAI_as_investment_caps_desc: "Limiting how much of a firm's capital can go to the mainland caps the damage Beijing can do to any one company."
+ TAI_as_exposure_monitor: "Monitor Mainland Exposure"
+ TAI_as_exposure_monitor_desc: "Tracking where our trade, investment and supplies depend on the mainland warns us before pressure arrives."
+ TAI_as_tighten_management: "Active Management, Effective Opening"
+ TAI_as_tighten_management_desc: "Reversing the order of the slogan puts risk management ahead of opening."
+ TAI_as_go_south: "Go South"
+ TAI_as_go_south_desc: "Investment in Southeast Asia spreads our factories across many countries instead of one."
+ TAI_as_three_links: "The Full Three Links"
+ TAI_as_three_links_desc: "Direct shipping, flights and mail would end decades of detours through Hong Kong. The economic gain is large, and so is the new dependence."
+ TAI_as_mainland_tourists: "Mainland Tourists"
+ TAI_as_mainland_tourists_desc: "Mainland tour groups bring money to hotels and shops, and Beijing can turn the flow off at will."
+ TAI_as_economic_framework: "A Cross-Strait Economic Framework"
+ TAI_as_economic_framework_desc: "A broad trade agreement would cut tariffs and open markets. Beijing would gain its strongest economic lever yet."
+ TAI_as_restore_1992_spirit: "Restore the Spirit of the 1992 Talks"
+ TAI_as_restore_1992_spirit_desc: "In 1992 the two sides agreed to set sovereignty aside and solve practical problems. We can return to that method without endorsing any one-China formula."
+ TAI_as_uphold_1992: "Uphold the 1992 Consensus"
+ TAI_as_uphold_1992_desc: "One China, respective interpretations: both sides affirm one China and each defines it differently. Beijing welcomes the formula; critics say it concedes too much."
+ TAI_as_sef_arats: "Revive the SEF-ARATS Channel"
+ TAI_as_sef_arats_desc: "The semi-official Straits Exchange Foundation and its mainland counterpart can resume talks on practical issues."
+ TAI_as_crisis_channel: "A Cross-Strait Crisis Channel"
+ TAI_as_crisis_channel_desc: "A standing line for incidents at sea and in the air lets both sides check facts before anyone escalates."
+ TAI_as_stabilization: "The Strait Stabilization Initiative"
+ TAI_as_stabilization_desc: "This alternate-history initiative offers restraint for restraint: we avoid unilateral constitutional change while Beijing reduces military coercion."
+ TAI_as_structured_restraint: "Structured Restraint"
+ TAI_as_structured_restraint_desc: "If Beijing answers our restraint with pressure, our patience becomes evidence for friends abroad."
+ TAI_as_cbms: "Military Confidence-Building Measures"
+ TAI_as_cbms_desc: "Advance notice of exercises and rules for close encounters lower the risk of accidental war."
+ TAI_as_one_country_each_side: "One Country on Each Side"
+ TAI_as_one_country_each_side_desc: "Declaring that there is one country on each side of the Strait thrills our base and alarms Beijing and Washington."
+ TAI_as_journey_of_peace: "The Journey of Peace"
+ TAI_as_journey_of_peace_desc: "Our party chairman can travel to Beijing to meet its leaders, the first such meeting since the civil war."
+ TAI_as_red_lines: "Know Beijing's Red Lines"
+ TAI_as_red_lines_desc: "Understanding what Beijing considers intolerable lets us choose our risks deliberately."
+ TAI_as_anti_secession: "Answer the Anti-Secession Law"
+ TAI_as_anti_secession_desc: "Beijing's new law authorises non-peaceful means under conditions it alone defines. Our answer can rally citizens or reassure friends."
+ TAI_as_assent: "The Assent of the People of Taiwan"
+ TAI_as_assent_desc: "No settlement across the Strait can take effect without the consent of the people who would live under it."
+ TAI_as_peace_accord: "A Cross-Strait Peace Accord?"
+ TAI_as_peace_accord_desc: "A formal peace accord could end the state of hostility. Any agreement would need a referendum, and voters may reject it."
+ TAI_as_status_quo_dividend: "The Status Quo Dividend"
+ TAI_as_status_quo_dividend_desc: "Calm in the Strait lowers insurance costs and attracts investors."
+ TAI_as_managed_ambiguity: "Managed Ambiguity"
+ TAI_as_managed_ambiguity_desc: "We decline to settle the final question while acting decisively to strengthen the state we already govern."
+ TAI_as_offshore_line: "Kinmen and Matsu Safety Line"
+ TAI_as_offshore_line_desc: "A direct line between local authorities on the offshore islands and Fujian handles fishing disputes and smuggling."
+ TAI_pl_root: "The Pacific Lifeline"
+ TAI_pl_root_desc: "Our friendships abroad are infrastructure for a crisis. They must be built before they are needed."
+ TAI_pl_washington: "Consult Washington"
+ TAI_pl_washington_desc: "Regular consultation helps Washington see our decisions coming."
+ TAI_pl_no_surprises: "No Surprises"
+ TAI_pl_no_surprises_desc: "We brief Washington before major announcements. It costs some freedom of action and earns trust."
+ TAI_pl_capitol_hill: "Friends on Capitol Hill"
+ TAI_pl_capitol_hill_desc: "Members of Congress from both parties support Taiwan's democracy. Their resolutions and visits keep us on Washington's agenda."
+ TAI_pl_transit: "Transit Diplomacy"
+ TAI_pl_transit_desc: "Presidential stopovers in American cities are not state visits, but they make headlines in both Taipei and Beijing."
+ TAI_pl_tifa: "Revive the TIFA Talks"
+ TAI_pl_tifa_desc: "The Trade and Investment Framework Agreement provides a forum to settle trade disputes with the United States."
+ TAI_pl_us_crisis_comms: "Crisis Communication with Washington"
+ TAI_pl_us_crisis_comms_desc: "Agreed channels for a crisis mean we can reach the right American officials in hours, not days."
+ TAI_pl_us_credit: "Pre-Arranged U.S. Credit Facility"
+ TAI_pl_us_credit_desc: "A standby facility can be requested in an emergency. Approval, terms and delivery would still be Washington's decision."
+ TAI_pl_tokyo: "Consult Tokyo: The Geographic Anchor"
+ TAI_pl_tokyo_desc: "Japan's southern islands lie close to ours, and its sea lanes run past us."
+ TAI_pl_japan_visa: "Visa-Free Japan"
+ TAI_pl_japan_visa_desc: "Visa-free travel brings tourists and business in both directions."
+ TAI_pl_japan_coast_guard: "Coast Guard Talks with Japan"
+ TAI_pl_japan_coast_guard_desc: "Our coast guards share waters, fishing disputes and search-and-rescue duties."
+ TAI_pl_japan_dialogue: "Unofficial Security Dialogue with Japan"
+ TAI_pl_japan_dialogue_desc: "Retired officials and scholars can discuss regional security without a formal alliance."
+ TAI_pl_japan_credit: "Japanese Credit Guarantees"
+ TAI_pl_japan_credit_desc: "Pre-arranged trade credit guarantees with Japanese lenders could keep imports flowing in a crisis."
+ TAI_pl_europe: "Europe's Commercial Stake"
+ TAI_pl_europe_desc: "European firms buy our chips and sell us machines. Their governments care about stability in the Strait."
+ TAI_pl_eu_trade: "EU Trade and Investment Talks"
+ TAI_pl_eu_trade_desc: "Investment and trade talks with the European Union diversify our partners."
+ TAI_pl_european_parliament: "Friends in the European Parliament"
+ TAI_pl_european_parliament_desc: "Resolutions supporting our participation in international bodies raise our profile in Europe."
+ TAI_pl_eu_supply: "European Industrial Supply Network"
+ TAI_pl_eu_supply_desc: "Long-term supply contracts with European manufacturers diversify where our machines and parts come from."
+ TAI_pl_india: "Look West to New Delhi"
+ TAI_pl_india_desc: "India's engineers and growing market make it a natural partner. This alternate-history diplomacy goes beyond our historical ties."
+ TAI_pl_india_tier1: "Tier I: Engineers and Electronics"
+ TAI_pl_india_tier1_desc: "Electronics assembly, packaging and engineering exchanges help both sides without risking our core technology."
+ TAI_pl_india_tier2: "Tier II: Controlled Licensing"
+ TAI_pl_india_tier2_desc: "Older process technology may be licensed under safeguards. Our crown jewels stay at home."
+ TAI_pl_india_market: "Indian Market Diversification"
+ TAI_pl_india_market_desc: "Indian customers reduce our reliance on any single export market."
+ TAI_pl_india_partnership: "Strategic Partnership with New Delhi"
+ TAI_pl_india_partnership_desc: "A broader partnership covers trade, technology and quiet security consultation."
+ TAI_pl_keep_allies: "Keep the Diplomatic Allies"
+ TAI_pl_keep_allies_desc: "Aid keeps the few states that recognise us on our side, at a steady cost and with scandal risks."
+ TAI_pl_end_checkbook: "End Checkbook Diplomacy"
+ TAI_pl_end_checkbook_desc: "Paying for recognition rewards the highest bidder. We will spend on real partnerships instead."
+ TAI_pl_transparent_aid: "Transparent Aid Diplomacy"
+ TAI_pl_transparent_aid_desc: "Published aid budgets and humanitarian projects earn respect rather than suspicion."
+ TAI_pl_wto: "Complete WTO Accession"
+ TAI_pl_wto_desc: "We applied as the Separate Customs Territory of Taiwan, Penghu, Kinmen and Matsu. Membership opens markets and exposes protected sectors."
+ TAI_pl_wha: "Bid for the World Health Assembly"
+ TAI_pl_wha_desc: "Observer status at the World Health Assembly would give our doctors direct access to global health information."
+ TAI_pl_sars: "Lessons of SARS"
+ TAI_pl_sars_desc: "SARS showed that exclusion from global health networks has real costs. Better surveillance and isolation wards will serve us in the next epidemic."
+ TAI_pl_technical_seats: "Technical Seats at the Table"
+ TAI_pl_technical_seats_desc: "Aviation, standards and scientific bodies matter in daily life even when sovereignty questions block full membership."
+ TAI_pl_apec: "Make APEC Count"
+ TAI_pl_apec_desc: "APEC is one of the few regional forums where we sit as a full member economy."
+ TAI_pl_offices: "Expand Representative Offices"
+ TAI_pl_offices_desc: "Economic and cultural offices abroad do the work of embassies without the name."
+ TAI_pl_document_coercion: "Prepare to Document Coercion"
+ TAI_pl_document_coercion_desc: "Careful records of every incident, published promptly, make it harder for Beijing to deny pressure."
+ TAI_pl_lifeline_holds: "The Lifeline Holds"
+ TAI_pl_lifeline_holds_desc: "Partners in Washington, Tokyo and Europe now have arrangements ready for a crisis. None of them is an automatic promise to fight."
+ TAI_bt_root: "Operation Blue Tiger"
+ TAI_bt_root_desc: "Defense, economy, diplomacy and democracy must now be planned as one national survival strategy. Our aim is to make Taiwan impossible to coerce at an acceptable price."
+ TAI_bt_accommodation: "Strategy: Accommodation"
+ TAI_bt_accommodation_desc: "We keep extensive economic ties and minimise confrontation. Prosperity grows, and so does Beijing's leverage."
+ TAI_bt_blue_tiger: "Strategy: Blue Tiger"
+ TAI_bt_blue_tiger_desc: "We keep selective ties while diversifying, strengthening partnerships and preparing for pressure."
+ TAI_bt_island_fortress: "Strategy: Island Fortress"
+ TAI_bt_island_fortress_desc: "We cut dependence quickly and stockpile heavily, accepting slower growth and a more alarmed Beijing."
+ TAI_bt_nsc: "The National Security Council Coordinates"
+ TAI_bt_nsc_desc: "Defense, economic, energy and foreign ministries plan crises together under one council."
+ TAI_bt_adaptation_office: "Economic Adaptation Office"
+ TAI_bt_adaptation_office_desc: "A standing office helps firms find new suppliers and markets before a crisis forces them to."
+ TAI_bt_count_the_days: "Count the Days"
+ TAI_bt_count_the_days_desc: "Every ministry reports how long its essential supplies would last under blockade."
+ TAI_bt_succession: "Unambiguous Succession"
+ TAI_bt_succession_desc: "Clear rules on who governs if leaders are killed or cut off deny an attacker a quick decapitation."
+ TAI_bt_alternate_seats: "Alternate Seats of Government"
+ TAI_bt_alternate_seats_desc: "Ministries keep secure backup sites and records outside Taipei."
+ TAI_bt_local_emergency: "Local Emergency Administration"
+ TAI_bt_local_emergency_desc: "County governments can run shelters, water and food distribution if the center is disrupted."
+ TAI_bt_emergency_limits: "Emergency Powers With Limits"
+ TAI_bt_emergency_limits_desc: "Emergency powers will be defined in law, time-limited and subject to legislative and judicial review."
+ TAI_bt_wan_an: "Revive the Wan An Drills"
+ TAI_bt_wan_an_desc: "The annual Wan An air-raid drills teach citizens where to shelter and how to help."
+ TAI_bt_medical_surge: "Emergency Medical Surge"
+ TAI_bt_medical_surge_desc: "Hospitals plan for mass casualties and epidemics with stockpiles and reserve staff."
+ TAI_bt_restore_grid: "Restore the Grid"
+ TAI_bt_restore_grid_desc: "Repair crews and spare transformers can bring power back quickly after an attack."
+ TAI_bt_redundant_comms: "Redundant Communications"
+ TAI_bt_redundant_comms_desc: "Backup radio, satellite and fiber links keep government and public informed when networks fail."
+ TAI_bt_financial_continuity: "Financial Continuity Plan"
+ TAI_bt_financial_continuity_desc: "Payment systems and banks rehearse working through outages and panics."
+ TAI_bt_rationing: "Rationing Without Panic"
+ TAI_bt_rationing_desc: "Fair, published rationing plans prevent hoarding if supplies run short."
+ TAI_bt_ports_open: "Keep the Ports Open"
+ TAI_bt_ports_open_desc: "Manual procedures let ports keep unloading ships if computer systems are attacked."
+ TAI_bt_airlift: "High-Value Airlift"
+ TAI_bt_airlift_desc: "Aircraft can carry small, valuable cargo such as chip materials and medicine, but never bulk fuel or food."
+ TAI_bt_emergency_procurement: "Emergency Procurement Networks"
+ TAI_bt_emergency_procurement_desc: "Pre-approved suppliers in third countries speed emergency purchases, with audits to catch fraud."
+ TAI_bt_publish_reserves: "Publish the Reserve Levels"
+ TAI_bt_publish_reserves_desc: "Regular, verified reports of fuel and food stocks take the air out of shortage rumours."
+ TAI_bt_document_incidents: "Document Every Incident"
+ TAI_bt_document_incidents_desc: "Every gray-zone incident is recorded and published with evidence."
+ TAI_bt_semiconductor_continuity: "Semiconductor Continuity Pact"
+ TAI_bt_semiconductor_continuity_desc: "The government and chipmakers agree how fabs, power and water will be protected in a crisis."
+ TAI_bt_counterweapon: "The Counterweapon"
+ TAI_bt_counterweapon_desc: "We prepare the option of restricting strategic chip exports to a coercer. Using it would cost us sales and push customers to build elsewhere."
+ TAI_bt_emergency_doctrine: "Blue Tiger Emergency Doctrine"
+ TAI_bt_emergency_doctrine_desc: "Emergency procedures for gray-zone pressure, blockade, missile attack and invasion are written, rehearsed and bounded by law."
+ TAI_bt_island_endures: "The Island Can Endure"
+ TAI_bt_island_endures_desc: "Citizens know the plans, the reserves are real and the government is trusted. Hardship need not become surrender."
+ TAI_bt_capstone: "Impossible to Coerce at an Acceptable Price"
+ TAI_bt_capstone_desc: "Taiwan does not have to become impossible to hurt. It has to become impossible to coerce at an acceptable price."
